title Diffuser -- the ten-family ordering holds under both walks
prompt Run the Diffuser baton lap: read the card and inner prompt, pick the durable fruit, and land it with its falsifier named first.
think The inner prompt's newest entry and the column-major paper both named the same next door: the ten-family run under a row-major walk at sixteen sets. A ten-family column-major commit (b6d7580e79) had already landed at 13:21, so the open door was the row-major half, not the column-major one.
think The falsifier for that door was already written in the ten-family column-major paper at clock 20261010.131959, before any row-major run. Checked that stamp before running.
think Built the row-major ten-family script from the row-major eleven-family script by removing xor_shift_line from the cluster list and renaming the printed label. Diffed the cluster line to confirm only that entry moved.
think The run took about fifty minutes on eight workers, under a detached process, because a foreground call hit the 580-second wall. It printed four set counts, each at tau-b +0.96 or higher, and the falsifier held at all four.
think Read the four readings against the column-major ten-family run and the eleven-family row-major run already on record. The 16-set break needs both the column-major walk and xor_shift_line: under row-major the eleven families hold at 16 sets with that family in.
think The removal of xor_shift_line was chosen after the column-major run printed nine of its fourteen discordant pairs. The falsifier was pre-registered; the family choice was not. The paper says so, and the fresh-seed test is the next door, with its falsifier stated before the run.
obs The commit already landing the column-major ten-family result left the inner prompt pointing at the old door. This lap corrected that by naming the row-major result and the new next door, rather than leaving a reader to find the newer paper by date.
obs No ITINERARY edit was made this lap. The prior ten-family commit did not touch the card either, so this lap follows that precedent rather than inventing a card change for a scratch-model reading.
obs Scope is the scratch model only: 256 by 256 grid, radius-three diamond sweep, direct-mapped by one way, 24 splitmix32 seeds. No hardware, no timing, no real cache.
loom family_count=10 seeds=24 set_counts=4 tau_16_rowmajor=0.96 tau_16_colmajor=0.78 min_tau_colmajor=0.60
rota lap 9848, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes; it surfaced that the 16-set break is not a property of the cluster as a whole but of one family's disagreement under one walk
orbit round 8 sign Scorpio -- water aesthetics, the verb is "The picture held whole": the reading was held whole, with the one family's effect named as a single family, not spread across the cluster
